      "title": "New, improved version of generic mapping tools released",
      "abstract": "<jats:p>Version 3.1 of the Generic Mapping Tools (GMT) has been released. More than 6000 scientists worldwide are currently using this free, public domain collection of UNIX tools that contains programs serving a variety of research functions. GMT allows users to manipulate (x,y) and (x,y,z) data, and generate PostScript illustrations, including simple x\u2010y diagrams, contour maps, color images, and artificially illuminated, perspective, and/or shaded\u2010relief plots using a variety of map projections (see <jats:italic>Wessel and Smith</jats:italic> [1991] and <jats:italic>Wessel and Smith</jats:italic> [1995], for details.). GMT has been installed under UNIX on most types of workstations and both IBM\u2010compatible and Macintosh personal computers.</jats:p>",
